## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical incident engineering: how to fuse disparate signals, assign accountability, and make safe change decisions under pressure.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-signal correlation across metrics/logs/traces
- SLO-aligned alert routing and ownership mapping
- Canary and synthetic testing for regression prevention
- RCA templating and rollback playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple rule mapping alerts to on-call owners
const owners = {
  payments: "team-payments",
  auth: "team-auth",
  inventory: "team-inventory"
};
function route(alert) {
  const svc = alert.tags?.service || "general";
  return owners[svc] || "oncall";
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the end-to-end runbook in a staging environment?
- What metrics would you collect to validate the success of the rollback strategy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests planning of safe, multi-region rollout with feature flags and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Progressive rollout
- Feature flags
- Telemetry and SLO-aligned signals
- Cache invalidation/versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for rollout gating
const enabled = getFlag("new_api_behavior");
if (enabled && regions.includes(currentRegion)) {
  useNewBehavior();
} else {
  useOldBehavior();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this if some regions have mandatory latency budgets?
- How would you integrate with an incident response playbook?
